<BaseLayout title="NEST privacy information — VCode" description="How NEST handles local preferences, Game Center and optional game features." lang="en" path="/en/nest/privacy/" alternatePath="/nest/privacy/">
  <article class="guide"><a class="back-link" href="/en/app-store/nest/">← NEST</a><header><p class="kicker">Privacy</p><h1>NEST</h1><p>A thoughtful strategy game with no advertising and no first-party user account. Updated 23 September 2026.</p></header><div class="guide-body">
    <h2>Local game settings</h2><p>NEST stores game settings and interface choices on your device. Optional assets for the on-device opponent may remain in the app’s storage. VCode does not send this data to its own server.</p>
    <h2>Game Center</h2><p>Online play, invitations, leaderboards and achievements use Apple Game Center. Apple manages Game Center sign-in and related data under its account and privacy practices.</p>
    <h2>Device motion</h2><p>If you choose dynamic board lighting, the game may ask for access to device motion data. The game remains fully usable when access is not granted.</p>
    <h2>Advertising and tracking</h2><p>The current release contains no advertising, advertising SDK or tracking across apps and websites.</p>
    <h2>Contact</h2><p>Send privacy questions to <a href="mailto:podpora@zeleznalady.cz">podpora@zeleznalady.cz</a>. Do not include passwords, access codes or information about other players.</p>
  </div></article>
</BaseLayout>
